From u57a7662e790ccc92 at groups.google.com  Sat Jun  4 20:59:43 2016
From: u57a7662e790ccc92 at groups.google.com (Shawn Garbett)
Date: Sat, 04 Jun 2016 20:59:43 +0000
Subject: Re: [simmer-devel] Issue resetting arrival times between each rep
Message-ID: <VJlGgyLou08.KFx69oVtBAAJ@simmer-devel.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <VJlGgyLou08.xO4DZcZsBAAJ@simmer-devel.groups.google.com>
References: <VJlGgyLou08.xO4DZcZsBAAJ@simmer-devel.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/simmer-devel/c/VJlGgyLou08/m/KFx69oVtBAAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

If arrivals are driven by an exponential distribution, this is "memoryless". I.e., you could draw arrivals based on this, then at some point redraw events that haven't occurred yet. So, one could have an event occurring on a set time that triggers a redraw. If the rates change at that point, it works out fine.

I'm driving our simulations via a main event loop. See: https://github.com/spgarbet/right/blob/master/simvastatin/simvastatin.R

This works since most of our events are exponential in our models.

