From u0f5b7adb7e70bd8b at groups.google.com  Thu Jun 16 13:55:00 2016
From: u0f5b7adb7e70bd8b at groups.google.com (=?utf-8?b?ScOxYWtpIMOaY2Fy?=)
Date: Thu, 16 Jun 2016 13:55:00 +0000
Subject: New feature: strict queue size
Message-ID: <hHbfbL5ItpE.Z_C0YtSFAwAJ@simmer-devel.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/simmer-devel/c/hHbfbL5ItpE/m/Z_C0YtSFAwAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hi all,

New option queue_size_strict for add_resource. By default, the behaviour does not change. But queue_size_strict=TRUE guarantees that queue_size is not exceeded with preemption enabled (see #59 <https://github.com/r-simmer/simmer/issues/59>).

Regards,
​
--
Iñaki Úcar
http://www.enchufa2.es
@Enchufa2 <https://twitter.com/#%21/Enchufa2>

